01:05:09.206 --> 01:05:12.073
He helped with archiving
dotty's research materials...


01:05:12.075 --> 01:05:14.075
At the magazine
after she died.


01:05:15.211 --> 01:05:17.345
What?


01:05:17.347 --> 01:05:20.548
Wait, wait, how?
How is that possible?


01:05:23.586 --> 01:05:25.620
Birds are my muses.


01:05:27.123 --> 01:05:31.326
And I strive to be
a true watcher.


01:05:31.328 --> 01:05:34.329
I can remember when I spotted my
first greater prairie chicken...


01:05:34.331 --> 01:05:36.197
But not
my own daughter's birthday.


01:05:36.199 --> 01:05:38.066
But you're already--


01:05:38.068 --> 01:05:40.635
I'm 63 years old
and very much alone.


01:05:40.637 --> 01:05:43.004
I guide assholes
for money.


01:05:43.006 --> 01:05:46.041
I have one leg
and no driver's license.


01:05:46.043 --> 01:05:48.543
Please do not confuse me
with a role model.


01:05:54.116 --> 01:05:56.318
Why don't you have
a driver's license?


01:05:56.320 --> 01:05:58.420
A bit of a mix-up...


01:05:58.422 --> 01:06:03.358
Between what I thought
was an albino nighthawk
and a high-speed police chase.


01:06:08.064 --> 01:06:09.631
Get your binoculars out.


01:06:09.633 --> 01:06:12.600
Okay, keep looking.
Keep looking.
See if you see it.


01:06:36.058 --> 01:06:37.559
Remarkable.


01:06:38.728 --> 01:06:41.262
Yeah, it's empty
though.


01:06:41.264 --> 01:06:42.764
Here goes nothin'.


01:06:50.273 --> 01:06:54.342
Was that it?
Maybe.
It was a little muffled.


01:06:54.344 --> 01:06:57.045
No, it was definitely
a greeting call.


01:06:57.047 --> 01:06:59.381
I think that maybe it was--
- oh, my god!


01:06:59.383 --> 01:07:02.384
That would be
a male mallard.
Oh.


01:07:02.386 --> 01:07:04.419
Wait.


01:07:04.421 --> 01:07:06.454
Why did it answer
to a scoter call?


01:07:07.590 --> 01:07:09.657
Maybe it was raised
by scoters.


01:07:09.659 --> 01:07:12.193
It was not raised
by scoters, okay?


01:07:14.730 --> 01:07:19.100
cross lake
is a few miles up. I think
maybe we should just go there.


01:07:19.102 --> 01:07:21.369
Why would it go
to the lake that's
farther from shore?


01:07:21.371 --> 01:07:24.239
It's not unheard of.
It's practically
unheard of.


01:07:24.241 --> 01:07:26.374
Guys?


01:07:26.376 --> 01:07:28.410
Is that your duck,
david?


01:07:36.452 --> 01:07:38.186
Oh, my god.


01:07:39.822 --> 01:07:41.456
What's it doing?


01:07:41.458 --> 01:07:43.558
Shh. It's preening.


01:07:46.395 --> 01:07:49.064
The light
couldn't be better.


01:07:49.066 --> 01:07:50.665
It's a magnificent bird.


01:08:23.466 --> 01:08:25.100
shit!


01:08:42.852 --> 01:08:44.886
Hey, fellas!
What the hell, man!


01:08:44.888 --> 01:08:47.222
I'm carl senior.


01:08:47.224 --> 01:08:49.157
This is my son,
carl junior.


01:08:49.159 --> 01:08:51.826
- oh, awesome!
You just shot an extinct duck!
- timmy, calm down.


01:08:51.828 --> 01:08:53.862
I'm not sure you know
what that word means.


01:08:53.864 --> 01:08:56.364
Your friend is nuts!


01:08:56.366 --> 01:08:58.633
Whoa.


01:08:58.635 --> 01:09:00.702
Easy, cruise.
hey.


01:09:03.272 --> 01:09:05.640

Whoa.


01:09:05.642 --> 01:09:08.376
- how did this happen?
- these morons shot it.


01:09:08.378 --> 01:09:11.779
Everyone, relax.
You shot
an extinct duck, sir.


01:09:11.781 --> 01:09:14.916
Does extinct mean
something different these days?



01:09:25.462 --> 01:09:27.362
It's suffering.


01:09:27.364 --> 01:09:30.565
Give it to me. Please.


01:09:32.601 --> 01:09:34.202
Please.


01:09:41.578 --> 01:09:44.379
May I see the animal?


01:09:52.555 --> 01:09:55.356
This isn't a labrador duck.
 what?


01:09:55.358 --> 01:09:59.260
Its neck does decline strangely,
but I think what we have here...


01:09:59.262 --> 01:10:01.963
Is an oddly-plumaged
hybrid mallard.


01:10:01.965 --> 01:10:05.400
- look at the wing markings.
- see, the wing markings
always concerned me.


01:10:05.402 --> 01:10:07.202
Yep. It's definitely
an odd hybrid of sorts.


01:10:07.204 --> 01:10:09.837
Just shut up, jeff.
If it's okay with you guys,


01:10:09.839 --> 01:10:12.540
we'd like to take the duck
for our banquet.


01:10:12.542 --> 01:10:15.376
Banquet?
We're hunting
for our church banquet.


01:10:15.378 --> 01:10:18.479
All the proceeds are going
to the save darfur foundation.


01:10:18.481 --> 01:10:21.849
Well, that's a bit
of silver lining.


01:10:21.851 --> 01:10:23.885
David, it's--


01:10:26.255 --> 01:10:28.289
david, it was just
a hybrid mallard.


01:10:45.841 --> 01:10:48.610
It looked at me.


01:10:52.481 --> 01:10:54.482
It didn't have to suffer.


01:10:55.451 --> 01:10:56.918
I know.


01:11:01.824 --> 01:11:03.858
Why did she have to die?


01:11:11.634 --> 01:11:13.668
I don't know why.


01:11:21.944 --> 01:11:24.946
<i>You know in   Indiana jones
and the temple of doom,</i>


01:11:24.948 --> 01:11:27.815
the bad guy that goes around
and rips the heart
out of people...


01:11:27.817 --> 01:11:30.718
And holds it up
in front of their face
so they watch it beat?


01:11:30.720 --> 01:11:33.788
Yeah,
I hate that part.



01:11:45.669 --> 01:11:48.670
I don't see how
it'll ever stop hurting.


01:11:51.840 --> 01:11:55.643
Well, um, maybe one day...


01:11:55.645 --> 01:12:00.748
It'll feel less awful
than "ripping an organ
out of your chest" pain.


01:12:02.484 --> 01:12:04.686
But my guess is
it'll always hurt.


01:12:13.562 --> 01:12:15.029
Yeah.


01:12:20.904 --> 01:12:23.404
Thank you.
You're welcome.


01:12:28.677 --> 01:12:31.379
What-what time is it?


01:12:31.381 --> 01:12:34.415
I don't know.
I think my phone died
three hours ago.


01:12:34.417 --> 01:12:36.017
Will we make it back
for the wedding?


01:12:36.019 --> 01:12:39.120
I mean, we don't have a car.
I wonder if I have
cell service.


01:12:40.422 --> 01:12:42.390
- oh, my god.
- what?


01:12:42.392 --> 01:12:44.459
What?
Oh, my god, no.


01:12:52.835 --> 01:12:55.570
This is--
this is worse
than it looks.


01:12:55.572 --> 01:12:57.472
we need to get you home.
yeah.


01:13:16.492 --> 01:13:18.760
So, those guys
weren't really drug lords.


01:13:18.762 --> 01:13:21.496
No, they were pretty much
the opposite of drug lords.


01:13:24.833 --> 01:13:26.934
You're not going
to taste that, are you?


01:13:29.471 --> 01:13:31.606
Just kidding.
It's rock candy.


01:13:31.608 --> 01:13:34.575
- I said it was rock candy!
- your first correct I.d.


01:13:34.577 --> 01:13:36.911
It's going on
my life list.


01:13:48.957 --> 01:13:51.025
<i>
Now we'll hear
a musical selection...</i>


01:13:51.027 --> 01:13:54.695
<i>From the son of the bride,
miguel santos.</i>


01:13:54.697 --> 01:13:56.164
Miguel?


01:14:04.173 --> 01:14:09.677
♪ Meet Me Tonight
In dreamland ♪


01:14:09.679 --> 01:14:14.482
♪ Under The Silv'ry Moon ♪


01:14:14.484 --> 01:14:19.554
♪ Meet Me Tonight
In dreamland ♪


01:14:19.556 --> 01:14:24.525
♪ Where Love's
Sweet roses bloom ♪


01:14:24.527 --> 01:14:28.095
♪ Meet Me In Dreamland ♪


01:14:28.097 --> 01:14:34.001
♪ Oh, Sweet Dreamy Dreamland ♪


01:14:34.003 --> 01:14:39.040
♪ There Make My Dreams ♪


01:14:39.042 --> 01:14:44.145
♪ Come True ♪


01:14:49.184 --> 01:14:51.652
Thank you, miguel.


01:14:51.654 --> 01:14:55.223
Mm! And now the rings.


01:14:55.225 --> 01:14:56.891
David?


01:15:07.836 --> 01:15:09.904
Working at
your own wedding?


01:15:09.906 --> 01:15:13.508
Right?
It's pretty messed up.


01:15:13.510 --> 01:15:15.877
You know, there's a million
people to talk to out there.


01:15:15.879 --> 01:15:19.113
I know. It's what I get
for hiring eric, I guess.


01:15:19.115 --> 01:15:21.883
That is what you get.


01:15:33.095 --> 01:15:35.062
Dad?


01:15:35.064 --> 01:15:36.764
Yeah?


01:15:40.102 --> 01:15:42.103
Were you seeing juliana...


01:15:43.872 --> 01:15:45.907
Before or after mom--


01:15:47.276 --> 01:15:49.176
definitely after.


01:15:53.682 --> 01:15:55.049
Good.


01:16:03.091 --> 01:16:06.060
Your mother
was the love of my life.


01:16:06.995 --> 01:16:08.796
You know that.


01:16:11.300 --> 01:16:13.067
No, I didn't.


01:16:16.772 --> 01:16:20.641
Oh, jesus christ!


01:16:22.311 --> 01:16:26.714
David, I'm sorry.
I should have done a better job
of explaining it all.


01:16:26.716 --> 01:16:28.649
We spoke about it.
No, we didn't.


01:16:28.651 --> 01:16:30.818
We didn't speak about it.
Not really.


01:16:31.753 --> 01:16:33.287
We didn't.


01:16:39.127 --> 01:16:42.863
You know, it's--
you remember that--


01:16:42.865 --> 01:16:45.366
I just don't want to pretend
that we don't Miss mom.


01:16:48.804 --> 01:16:50.237
Me either.


01:16:56.044 --> 01:16:58.112
Wanna grab that chicken?


01:17:09.992 --> 01:17:12.927
They thought we were
terrorists. It was awful.


01:17:12.929 --> 01:17:15.363
Hey. Excuse me.


01:17:15.365 --> 01:17:17.832
Are you in a band
or something?


01:17:17.834 --> 01:17:19.266
Excuse me?


01:17:30.012 --> 01:17:32.713
Hello?


01:17:34.283 --> 01:17:37.151
Hey!



01:17:37.153 --> 01:17:39.286
Hey, everyone. Um--


01:17:40.922 --> 01:17:43.791
so technically
I'm the best man here,


01:17:44.993 --> 01:17:47.828
and I guess
I'm supposed to give a toast.


01:17:47.830 --> 01:17:50.331
Um--


01:17:50.333 --> 01:17:52.900

Where do I start?
The thing is,


01:17:54.436 --> 01:17:58.906
the last couple of days
I've been looking
for an extinct duck.


01:17:58.908 --> 01:18:00.941
No.


01:18:00.943 --> 01:18:03.678
No, it's not like
a metaphor or something.


01:18:03.680 --> 01:18:06.013
Turns out
it wasn't extinct.


01:18:06.015 --> 01:18:08.849
Actually, it wasn't the duck
I thought it was,


01:18:08.851 --> 01:18:10.818
and it got shot,


01:18:10.820 --> 01:18:13.220
uh, but in a weird way,
it turns out...


01:18:13.222 --> 01:18:17.024
It might actually
help the whole situation
going on in darfur.


01:18:18.026 --> 01:18:20.094
Sorry. Anyway--


01:18:23.166 --> 01:18:26.834
I'm-i'm glad
I made it here... Today.


01:18:27.969 --> 01:18:30.071
Well, the last few years
have been--


01:18:31.373 --> 01:18:33.841
they've been kind of rough
for our family.


01:18:33.843 --> 01:18:35.443
Um--


01:18:36.445 --> 01:18:39.246
david--
I know. Sorry.


01:18:39.248 --> 01:18:41.315
Dad likes to fill holes
with lists.


01:18:41.317 --> 01:18:43.851
That's what he does.


01:18:43.853 --> 01:18:47.455
He writes lists of everything,
like lists of lists,


01:18:47.457 --> 01:18:52.426
and I like to find
rare birds, so I'm not
really one to talk, but...


01:18:52.428 --> 01:18:56.363
It doesn't--
doesn't really work.


01:18:56.365 --> 01:19:01.102
Which is why
I'm so glad he found juliana.


01:19:01.104 --> 01:19:04.872
Because I know my mom
really liked her...


01:19:04.874 --> 01:19:08.075
And my dad
obviously likes her too.


01:19:09.911 --> 01:19:11.946
That's all that matters.


01:19:13.882 --> 01:19:16.117
And...


01:19:16.119 --> 01:19:18.119
That's why
we're all here, right?


01:19:21.156 --> 01:19:22.857
So...


01:19:24.392 --> 01:19:27.962
I wish them a happy
and long life together.


01:19:27.964 --> 01:19:29.930
Here's to dad and juliana.


01:19:42.043 --> 01:19:44.245
You were perfect.


01:20:03.299 --> 01:20:06.967
So, does eric know
that we, like,
destroyed his engine?


01:20:08.403 --> 01:20:10.337

Uh, you know,


01:20:11.406 --> 01:20:13.240
timing's not quite right.


01:20:13.242 --> 01:20:15.476
Yeah, he's not
gonna be happy.


01:20:15.478 --> 01:20:20.514
I got some serious shit on him
that I've been saving
for a moment like this.


01:20:20.516 --> 01:20:22.249
Got it.


01:20:22.251 --> 01:20:25.152
Think I'm gonna
head home now.
Yeah, me too.


01:20:26.421 --> 01:20:28.522
Good times!


01:20:28.524 --> 01:20:30.224
Totally.


01:20:37.265 --> 01:20:40.367
Bye.


01:20:40.369 --> 01:20:43.170

So how long should I wait
till I call kim?


01:20:43.172 --> 01:20:45.973
What,
you got her number?
Yeah. 


01:20:45.975 --> 01:20:47.942
Why didn't you
tell me that, dude?


01:20:47.944 --> 01:20:50.211
I should go too.


01:20:50.213 --> 01:20:52.179
I guess.


01:20:52.181 --> 01:20:55.382
So, weirdly enough,
I had a lot of fun
this weekend.


01:20:55.384 --> 01:20:57.518
So did I.


01:20:57.520 --> 01:20:59.620
Peter gave me
his old pair.


01:20:59.622 --> 01:21:02.456
They're not as good as yours,
but I'm kinda getting the--


01:21:05.627 --> 01:21:07.161
hi.


01:21:15.003 --> 01:21:18.472
So, um... I guess
I'll see you tomorrow.


01:21:18.474 --> 01:21:21.108
Yeah. Okay.
Definitely.


01:21:24.379 --> 01:21:26.146
Bye. Yeah. Bye.
See ya.


01:21:30.252 --> 01:21:34.455
<i>
♪ It's Too Late Now
To rush apart ♪</i>


01:21:34.457 --> 01:21:38.359
<i>♪ Your Aching Heart
Wasn't on fire ♪</i>


01:21:38.361 --> 01:21:42.396
<i>♪ And If You Drain
The fluid from ♪</i>


01:21:42.398 --> 01:21:46.333
<i>♪ My Screaming Lungs,
I know I'll die ♪</i>


01:21:49.070 --> 01:21:52.006
<i>♪ And It's Hard To Know
What's right ♪</i>


01:21:53.008 --> 01:21:55.609
<i>♪ I Need You Tonight ♪</i>


01:21:57.012 --> 01:22:01.916
<i>♪ You Need Me Tonight ♪</i>


01:22:10.926 --> 01:22:14.061
<i>♪ It's Too Late Now
To hold on to the crutch ♪</i>


01:22:14.063 --> 01:22:16.297
<i>♪ When You Open Arms
And open hearts ♪</i>


01:22:16.299 --> 01:22:19.099
<i>♪ They Never Open Much ♪</i>


01:22:19.101 --> 01:22:23.070
<i>♪ If I Drain The Beauty From ♪</i>


01:22:23.072 --> 01:22:26.640
<i>♪ Your Beating Blood,
I know I'll die ♪</i>


01:22:26.642 --> 01:22:29.944
<i>♪ No ♪</i>


01:22:29.946 --> 01:22:34.048
<i>♪ I Never Try To ♪</i>


01:22:41.656 --> 01:22:44.024
<i>♪ But It's All Been Done ♪</i>


01:22:44.026 --> 01:22:47.394
<i>♪ We'll Hold On Tight ♪</i>


01:22:47.396 --> 01:22:50.731
<i>♪ I Will Hold Onto You ♪</i>


01:22:50.733 --> 01:22:55.669
<i>♪ And The Feeling
Of an empty love ♪</i>


01:22:55.671 --> 01:23:00.007
<i>♪ While I Hold Onto You ♪</i>


01:23:00.009 --> 01:23:07.481
<i>♪ And My Lord
I know it's true ♪</i>


01:23:30.271 --> 01:23:34.241
<i>
♪ And I've Been A-walkin'
Down that road ♪</i>


01:23:34.243 --> 01:23:39.546
<i>♪ And I Can Feel
The wind between my toes ♪</i>


01:23:40.548 --> 01:23:43.784
<i>♪ The Water, Oh, So Sweet ♪</i>


01:23:46.721 --> 01:23:51.225
<i>♪ And I Been Thinkin'
Maybe it's right ♪</i>


01:23:51.227 --> 01:23:56.030
<i>♪ And I Can Finally
Feel the things I love ♪</i>


01:23:57.032 --> 01:23:59.733
<i>♪ Shiver When You Talk ♪</i>


01:24:02.670 --> 01:24:06.640
<i>♪ Do Your Lips Feel All Of
The things that mine do? ♪</i>


01:24:06.642 --> 01:24:12.413
<i>♪ Do You Feel That Tingle
Inside of your shoe? ♪</i>


01:24:14.249 --> 01:24:16.550
<i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>


01:24:19.287 --> 01:24:23.657
<i>♪ And Nothin's ♪</i>


01:24:23.659 --> 01:24:25.826
<i>♪ Wrong ♪</i>


01:24:25.828 --> 01:24:29.196
<i>♪ It's Just Love ♪</i>


01:24:32.200 --> 01:24:36.370
<i>♪ And I've Been Hurt
And my heart's empty ♪</i>


01:24:36.372 --> 01:24:39.807
<i>♪ Soakin' In It
That is tempting ♪</i>


01:24:39.809 --> 01:24:42.476
<i>♪ But ♪</i>


01:24:42.478 --> 01:24:45.479
<i>♪ That All Floats Away ♪</i>


01:24:47.549 --> 01:24:50.551
<i>♪ And My Heart's
Been breakin' ♪</i>


01:24:50.553 --> 01:24:52.653
<i>♪ Like A Biscuit ♪</i>


01:24:52.655 --> 01:24:56.857
<i>♪ You Are The One
Who can finally fix it ♪</i>


01:24:58.593 --> 01:25:01.528
<i>♪ Will We Both Be Okay? ♪</i>


01:25:04.365 --> 01:25:08.368
<i>♪ Do You Look At Our Hands
And see that they're creased ♪</i>


01:25:08.370 --> 01:25:14.108
<i>♪ From A Trembling Here
That cannot be released ♪</i>


01:25:15.710 --> 01:25:18.212
<i>♪ Ee-ee-ee-eee ♪</i>


01:25:20.782 --> 01:25:25.185
<i>♪ Nothing's ♪</i>


01:25:25.187 --> 01:25:27.221
<i>♪ Wrong ♪</i>


01:25:27.223 --> 01:25:30.424
<i>♪ It's Just Love ♪</i>


01:25:33.361 --> 01:25:37.364
<i>♪ Nothing's ♪</i>


01:25:37.366 --> 01:25:39.500
<i>♪ Wrong ♪</i>


01:25:39.502 --> 01:25:42.636
<i>♪ It's Just Love ♪</i>


01:25:49.711 --> 01:25:53.614
<i>♪ It's Just ♪</i>


